### Code Quality Tools

- Implement ESLint with appropriate rulesets:
  - React hooks rules
  - TypeScript rules
  - Accessibility rules
  - Testing library rules
- Use Prettier for consistent code formatting:
  - No parentheses for single-parameter arrow functions
  - Omit semicolons
  - Use single quotes
  - Disable trailing commas
- Apply husky and lint-staged for pre-commit quality checks
- Enforce meaningful commit messages with commitlint

### Code Reviews

- Establish clear code review guidelines:
  - Functional correctness
  - Code quality and style
  - Performance considerations
  - Security best practices
- Utilize Merge Request templates for structured reviews

### Continuous Integration

- Set up CI/CD pipelines:
  - Check for code style consistency
  - Run tests and generate coverage reports
  - Enforce lint and type checking
  - Audit dependencies for vulnerabilities
  - Enforce commit message format
- Implement automated UI testing with screenshot comparisons
- Use deployment previews for visual verification
